thunderbolt-net (0.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  This version installs /usr/lib/modprobe.d/thunderbolt-net.conf, which
  enables rx_segment=1 rx_segment_mtu=1500 rx_page_pool=1 the next time
  thunderbolt_net is loaded. Earlier versions left these options off unless
  you created opt-in files in /etc/modprobe.d.

  To keep them off, copy the file to /etc/modprobe.d/thunderbolt-net.conf and
  edit the copy before reloading the module or rebooting. A file of the same
  name in /etc replaces the package file; files with other names that sort
  before it do not override it. The old opt-in files
  /etc/modprobe.d/thunderbolt-net-rx.conf and thunderbolt-net-page-pool.conf
  set the same values and can be removed.

 -- Shun Li <riverscn@gmail.com>  Sat, 10 Oct 2026 14:25:29 +0000
